  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WASH intervention and rehabilitation of educational centers to benefit children, families, and communities in 8 municipalities of Pinar del R&#xed;o.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide WASH and education assistance to communities affected by Hurricane Ian in western Cuba. This UNICEF project provides safe access to water and education to vulnerable people. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 184,110 people, including 78,489 women, 72,449 men, 33,172 children, and including 9,690 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
